 {
  "coord": "36:8",
  "verdict": "FAIL",
  "category": "hedge",
  "note": "\"seemed to have planned it\" adds a seeming; \"designing Providence\" is a flat statement.",
  "replacement": "“She’ll bring you a plate, and you will share my dinner. There’s always enough for two, even three.” Edna had meant to be as indifferent and reserved as he was when she met him. She had reached that decision through a laborious train of reasoning, in one of her despondent moods. But her resolve melted when she saw him, whom a designing Providence had led into her path."
 },
